  "question": {
    "text": "The cosine of the angle between any two diagonals of a cube is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the direction ratio's of two diagonals of a cube are\r\n(1,1,1) and (-1,1,1) $\\begin{aligned} \\therefore \\cos \\theta &=\\frac{a_{1} a_{2}+b_{1} b_{2}+c_{f} c_{2}}{\\sqrt{a_{1}^{2}+b_{1}^{2}+c_{1}^{2}} \\sqrt{a_{2}^{2}+b_{2}^{2}+c_{2}^{2}}} \\\\ &=\\frac{(1) \\times(-1)+(1) \\times(1)+(1) \\times(1)}{\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}}} \\\\ &=\\frac{-1+1+1}{\\sqrt{3} \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{1}{3} \\end{aligned}$"
  }
}